# Round 86.  SIX files, written by the chief in one edit for the same reason
# round 84 records: lanes do not write their own allowlist lines, because two
# lanes editing this file in the same round is how round 81 lost three of them.
# Both lanes of this round independently reported being ignored before commit,
# which is the fifth consecutive round the check-ignore step has paid for itself.
# It said FIVE until round 87 counted them.  Round 86 was cut off mid-flight and
# the round that took over re-ran the check-ignore step rather than trusting the
# sentence above, which is the only reason the sixth file below is here: the
# headless replay was listed in HYP-PF-023's evidence_refs while being invisible
# to version control, so the ledger would have cited a file a fresh clone does
# not contain.  The lesson is not "write six instead of five", it is that a
# prose count of allowlist lines is not a check, and the check is cheap.
# RUNTIMERES-ENCODER-001 -- the spawn-then-kill encoder's verifier, its report
# and the headless replay that drives the sweep over a real socket.
