# client has ever been shown an unsolicited 0x709E push.
!/tools/pf_logout_chat_push_headless_replay.py

# GO-LIVE (chief round 103, Panya order 2026-08-20 ~12:30).  The deny-all rule on
# line one hid the entire .github/ directory: the Windows gate workflow existed
# on disk but was never tracked, so a push would have carried no CI and Actions
# would never have run once.  A negation cannot re-include a file whose parent
# directory is excluded, so the directory itself is reopened first.
!/.github/
!/.github/**

# ---- subagent definitions, so a cloud round has the same specialists a bridge
# round had.  Claude Code picks these up automatically from the cloned repo.
# Both lines are needed: line 1 of this file is `/*`, and git does not descend
# into a directory it has already excluded.
!/.claude/
!/.claude/**

# SKIP-CENSUS-001 (chief round 106, Panya order 2026-08-20 ~15:45).  Actions run
# #3 was the first time this suite ran anywhere but Panya's bridge, and four
# tests went red reaching for evidence a fresh clone cannot have - FINDINGS R12
# measured on a second machine at last.  The repair is a declared skip, and the
# danger a declared skip introduces is that a real test drifts into the skip pile
# unnoticed, so every allowed skip is pinned by module and count and the census
# below is red when a count moves in either direction.  tests/ and docs/ are
# already allow-listed wholesale, so only the tool needs a line here.
!/tools/pf_pytest_precondition_census.py

